@startuml D3_Flow1_Architecture_Tools_Context
' ============================================================
' DOMAIN 3 — FLOW 1: What Claude Code Is + Tools + Setup +
' Context + Permission Modes  (Topics 1–5)
' CORE SPINE: agentic CLI -> plan/act loop -> tools -> context
' budget -> permission mode gates every action.
' EXAM-CRITICAL ORDERING: pre-tool-use HOOK fires FIRST,
' THEN permission check, THEN the tool runs.
' ============================================================
title Domain 3 · Flow 1 — Architecture, Tools, Setup, Context, Permission Modes (T1–5)\n(Agentic CLI -> plan/act loop -> tool -> context budget -> mode gate)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF6CC

start

' ---------- TOPIC 1: WHAT CLAUDE CODE IS ----------
partition "T1 · What Claude Code IS" {
  :You run `claude` in your TERMINAL\ne.g. "fix the failing tests";
  #LightCyan:It opens files, edits them, runs the test\ncommand, reads errors, fixes again — autonomously;
  note right
    == THE ONE BIG IDEA ==
    Claude Code = an AGENTIC CLI. "Claude with hands."
    * NOT a chat window, NOT autocomplete
    * Contractor you hand a key to  (vs Copilot = spell-checker)
    * Runs ARBITRARY bash, reads any permitted file,
      edits across MANY files in one task
    * Copilot/plugins have NO shell access
  end note
}

' ---------- THE PLAN / ACT LOOP ----------
partition "T1 · The Plan / Act Loop" {
  repeat
    :PLAN — decide next step;
    :TOOL CALL — do it;
    :OBSERVE — read the result;
    note right
      Loop = Plan -> Tool call -> Observe -> loop.
      This loop is what enables SELF-CORRECTION
      (vs a single-shot answer that can't recover).
    end note
  repeat while (Done or need clarification?) is (NO — keep going)
  ->YES;
}

' ---------- CONTEXT WINDOW ----------
partition "T1/T4 · Context Window (finite, shared budget)" {
  :History + every tool result + CLAUDE.md\nALL compete for the SAME finite window;
  note right
    == CONTEXT BUDGET ==
    * Verbose CLAUDE.md STEALS space from code + tool output
    * When it fills: content is COMPACTED (summarised),
      not silently deleted, not a crash
    == MEMORY / STATELESSNESS ==
    * New sessions do NOT auto-recall
    * ONLY DISK survives between sessions
    * CLAUDE.md loaded ONCE at session start, then RESIDENT
      all session (re-sent behind the scenes each turn)
    * Close terminal -> history gone; only disk persists
  end note
}

' ---------- TOPIC 2: TOOL SYSTEM ----------
partition "T2 · The Tool System (9 built-ins, task-driven each loop step)" {
  #LightYellow:Pick the right tool for THIS step;
  note right
    == 9 BUILT-IN TOOLS ==
    Read   — view a file (files, NOT dirs; use Bash `ls`); zero risk
    Write  — create new / full rewrite (overwrites ALL lines)
    Edit   — surgical change to lines (other lines untouched)
    Bash   — any shell cmd; most powerful + most dangerous, no undo
    Glob   — find files by NAME pattern (all *.test.ts)
    Grep   — search TEXT inside files (where payments API is called)
    WebSearch — close a knowledge gap (library changed after cutoff)
    WebFetch  — pull a specific URL you supply
    Agent  — spawn a SUB-AGENT with its OWN context window
    ----
    EXAM TRAP — Edit vs Write is NOT code-vs-noncode:
    50-line config, change port 3000->8000 ->
    Edit fixes 1 line, keeps 49; Write overwrites all 50.
    Read-before-Edit avoids stale assumptions.
  end note
}

' ---------- TOPIC 3: STARTING A PROJECT / /init ----------
partition "T3 · Starting a Project · /init" {
  :Run `claude` from PROJECT ROOT\n(root = default scope boundary);
  :Run `/init` -> auto-generates a STARTER CLAUDE.md;
  note right
    /init detects 4 things:
    1. project name  2. key files / entry points
    3. languages & frameworks  4. suggested rules
    ----
    EXAM POINT: /init output is a STARTING POINT,
    never a finished config. Review REQUIRED:
    * verify stack (misreads polyglot repos)
    * add what it can't infer (branching, security paths,
      team conventions, coverage)
    * remove noise (every line costs the window)
    Shipping the raw draft = a liability.
  end note
}

' ---------- TOPIC 4: MANAGING CONTEXT ----------
partition "T4 · Adding & Managing Context" {
  :4 ways context enters (all spend the SAME budget):\nfile path · @-refs · pasted URL · inline instructions;
  if (Does this content CHANGE what Claude would do?) then (YES)
    #LightGreen:INCLUDE — targeted (the 2 files that matter);
    note left
      TARGETED INCLUSION = a HABIT (a dial).
      Include: architecture decisions, conventions,
      test rules, known constraints, security paths.
      Small accurate context BEATS large noisy one.
    end note
  else (NO — noise / secret / build artifact)
    #Pink:EXCLUDE via DENY RULE in settings.json;
    note right
      DENY RULES = a GUARDRAIL (a wall).
      Dual purpose (both get tested):
      1. SECURITY — .env can NEVER enter the session
      2. EFFICIENCY — no node_modules / build output
      ----
      FILE SEPARATION TRAP:
      deny rules live in settings.json, NOT CLAUDE.md.
      CLAUDE.md = instructions (can be ignored/forgotten)
      settings.json = permissions (enforced pre-tool)
    end note
  endif
  :Compaction: when full, Claude SUMMARISES older\nturns (gist survives, verbatim doesn't);
  note right
    Two triggers: auto near the limit, or `/compact`.
    Put a COMPACT INSTRUCTION in CLAUDE.md naming
    what must always survive (a task ID / file path).
  end note
}

' ---------- TOPIC 5: PERMISSION MODES + THE GATE ORDER ----------
partition "T5 · Permission Modes (session-wide dial)" {
  :A pending Edit / Bash / etc. is about to run;

  #Orange:GATE 1 — pre-tool-use HOOK fires FIRST;
  note right
    ============================================
    EXAM-CRITICAL ORDERING (both are pre-exec gates):
      pre-tool-use HOOK  ->  PERMISSION check  ->  tool runs
    Hook is CODE YOU control; permission is config you SET.
    ============================================
  end note

  #Orange:GATE 2 — PERMISSION check (by mode + deny rules);
  note right
    == 6 MODES ==
    default      — reads free; every edit/cmd ASKS (safest)
    accept edits — writes in working dir w/o asking; review via git diff
    plan         — read-only; proposes; on approve EXITS into chosen mode
    don't ask    — auto-DENIES anything not pre-approved (locked pipelines)
    bypass       — skips prompts ENTIRELY (isolated container/VM only)
    auto         — cuts routine prompts BUT a CLASSIFIER reviews each action
    ----
    3 anchors: mode is SESSION-WIDE · only the WORKING DIR is
    auto-approvable · PROTECTED paths (.git, Claude's config)
    are never auto-approved.
    Switch: shift+tab cycles default->accept edits->plan;
    or a launch flag; or a settings default. You set it via
    CONTROLS, not by asking Claude in chat.
    ----
    auto vs bypass: bypass has NOTHING watching;
    auto has a SUPERVISOR classifier that blocks escalation.
  end note

  if (Allowed by hook AND permission?) then (YES)
    #LightGreen:Tool RUNS;
  else (NO)
    #Pink:BLOCKED before any effect;
  endif
}

stop

floating note left
  == FLOW 1 SPINE ==
  Agentic CLI -> Plan/Act loop -> pick a TOOL ->
  everything shares one CONTEXT budget ->
  every action passes HOOK then PERMISSION.
  ----
  == HIGH-YIELD FACTS ==
  * Loop = Plan/Tool/Observe -> self-correction
  * Only DISK survives sessions
  * Edit = surgical; Write = full overwrite
  * /init = starter, never finished
  * deny rules -> settings.json (NOT CLAUDE.md)
  * ORDER: hook -> permission -> tool
  * auto = supervised; bypass = unsupervised
end note

@enduml
